                <pb facs="0512" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3080a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-25T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department is with difficulty restraining responsible press comment here on
                    the Tientsin affair and is doubtful how long it may be able to do so owing to
                    the numerous circumstantial reports arriving in the United States through papers
                    published in China and Japan. An early settlement of the question is highly
                    desirable. I have spoken to Ishii in the same sense.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
